**Engagement Title: Liquid Credit Technical Consultant**

**Location: Hyderabad, India (Hybrid Schedule; 3 days in office)**

**Working Hours: 4 PM to 1 AM IST**

**Assignment Duration: 12 months**

**Engaging Team's Highlights**

The ideal candidate should have experience within an asset management firm, with a strong preference for a fixed income or liquid credit background over pure equities experience. They should have hands-on experience with fixed income performance and attribution, portfolio-level reporting such as portfolio summaries and factsheets, and a solid understanding of fixed income analytics and metrics, including spreads, yields, and duration. The role will also require someone who can confidently address technical fixed income questions for RFPs and DDQs, often within short turnaround times.

From a technical standpoint, SQL is a must-have, while Power BI and Python are strong pluses. Experience with Bloomberg PORT and FactSet, as well as exposure to portfolio construction, is also beneficial.

Certifications such as FRM or CIPM would be a strong fit, and progress toward the CFA (Levels I III) is preferred but not required.

**Scope And Responsibilities**

The Risk & Reporting department is responsible for delivering best-in-class, technology-enabled analyses and reporting to clients' current and prospective investors and portfolio management professionals globally.

The Associate will serve as a subject matter expert on the instruments and markets clients participate in, with an emphasis on liquid credit (Investment Grade, High Yield, Bank Debt, Convertibles, and Structured Credit). The incumbent will support portfolio construction, risk analysis, and quantitative insight.

This role requires deep subject matter expertise in leveraged credit markets and a strong understanding of fixed income investment analytics, reporting, and data architecture. The successful candidate will help lead cross-functional efforts across investment, data, and technology teams, and will advocate for the value of quantitative investment strategies throughout the organisation. The team is really looking for tech-heavy profiles with a Fixed Income background.

**Scope includes**

* Designing and interpreting fixed income attribution, portfolio construction, and risk models & analysis to support portfolio construction and performance analysis;
* Serving as the go-to resource for portfolio managers on risk, construction, and analytical questions; helping ensure seamless coordination across portfolio operations, data flows, and investment implementation processes;
* Translating complex quantitative models into clear insights for investment teams and senior leadership;
* Leading the build-out and maintenance of reporting infrastructure using SQL, Python, Power BI, and cloud-based tools;
* Collaborating with Business Analysts and IT to improve data systems, pipelines, and automation capabilities;
* Supporting firm-wide understanding of RR&A deliverables, data environments, and third-party data sources (e.g., FactSet, Bloomberg); and
* Ensuring analytical output is accurate, consistent, and aligned with the client's investment philosophy.
* Fixed income strategies: Working Knowledge of IG, HY, leveraged loans, and structured credit strategies
* Reporting: Recurring reports, Ad hoc analysis, RFPs, and DDQs

**Partnership & Innovation**

* Collaborate with organisational partners to produce and advance R&P deliverables: Investment/Portfolio Management, Product Specialists, Investor Relations, Marketing and business development, Accounting, IT, and Compliance;
* Evolve strategy and portfolio reporting suite in response to new strategies and investor needs; Support strategy-level tactical projects through collaboration with other team members and key stakeholders.

**Experience Required**

* Experience at an asset management, investment bank, or other financial institution focused on fixed income or credit analytics;
* In-depth understanding of investment-grade, high-yield bonds, leveraged loans, and the broader leveraged credit market;
* Experience with fixed income attribution and portfolio risk models; familiarity with tools like FactSet, Bloomberg, and proprietary analytics platforms;
* Strong technical proficiency, including advanced SQL and Python, and experience building reports in Power BI;
* Understanding of cloud data architectures and large-scale data workflows;
* Experience managing cross-functional projects and communicating with stakeholders across investment and technology teams
* Tech stack (must): Hands-on SQL + Power BI (Must) and Python (good to have) to build scalable reporting, automation, dashboards, and analytics infrastructure
* Process improvement: Ability to combine FI analytics, credit market knowledge, and automation to support best-in-class investor and portfolio reporting - Portfolio Summaries, Factsheets
* Portfolio analytics: Yields, Spreads, Duration, and other core FI risk/return metrics

Job Summary :

Medpace is a Clinical Research Organization that is rapidly growing across the globally. Due to our continued growth, we are in search of qualified and focused individuals for a vital role in our Core Lab department. Our Clinical Application Support provides multi Tiers support for clinical research and core lab platforms across Medical Imaging, ECG, connected medical devices, mobile applications, and virtualized workstations.This position will deliver timely, high-quality customer service to globally located end users and investigator sites by troubleshooting technical and workflow issues, tracking incidents through resolution, and performing software installation and validation activities. In addition, you will act as a key liaison between end users, internal development teams, core infrastructure teams, and external vendors to coordinate escalations and ensure seamless operations across clinical trials.

Responsibilities :

* Provide technical support for clinical research and core lab platforms, including Medical Imaging, ECG, connected medical devices, mobile applications, and virtualized workstations;
* Deliver timely, high-quality customer service to internal users, central readers and investigator sites located globally;
* Troubleshoot and resolve technical and workflow issues, escalating to the appropriate teams when needed;
* Log, track, and document incidents and service requests through resolution using the ticketing system;
* Perform software installation, configuration, testing, and validation activities in accordance with company procedures;
* Act as a liaison between end users, internal development teams, core infrastructure teams, and external vendors while maintaining the interests of end users;
* Coordinate escalations and follow up with stakeholders to ensure seamless operations across clinical trials;
* Create and maintain support documentation, knowledge base articles, and user guides;
* Ensure support activities comply with applicable regulatory standards (GCP, 21 CFR Part 11, HIPAA/GDPR); and
* Perform other system-related tasks to meet company objectives.

Qualifications :

* Bachelor's degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Biomedical Engineering, Life Sciences, or a related field (or equivalent experience);
* 1–3 years of application or technical support experience, preferably in a CRO, pharmaceutical, or clinical research environment;
* Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities;
* Excellent communication skills and ability to work cross-functionally with staff, vendors, and external users from multiple countries;
* Good organizational skills, very detail oriented, and flexible;
* Must be able to work concurrently on several issues and projects, each with specific requirements;
* Competent in installation and troubleshooting of software;
* Demonstrated ability to learn new technologies/applications; and
* Knowledge of Microsoft® Windows operating systems.

**Preferred Qualifications**

* Hands-on familiarity with virtualized environments, mobile/device support, and ticketing systems; and
